  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "terminal-ferry",
      "id": "LUG-15",
      "plano": "terminal-ferry",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.IDd94316DhSx3ptV]{The Ferry Terminal and the Last Ferry}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.doItxeK8y7M1PufU.JournalEntryPage.tG1m5PTkmBA1pvmc]{A4-E03 · The Last Ferry}</p>\n<p><strong>A4-E03, 12:55 a.m.</strong> “The terminal is almost empty under the fluorescents. A guard looks at his phone; a coffee machine blinks behind an ‘out of service’ sign. Outside, the last ferry of the night waits with every light on, like a four-story white building floating on black water. The horn sounds once, long. On the passenger ramp, an old man in a dark suit with an aluminum briefcase climbs slowly, leaning on the arm of an enormous man who looks back and sniffs the air.”</p>\n<p><strong>The waiting room</strong> is on the upper floor. Fixed <strong>benches</strong> in three double rows; a handful of sleepy-looking passengers (tokens). The <strong>security guard</strong> is at his podium beside the <strong>boarding door</strong> (west), looking at his phone. The <strong>broken coffee machine</strong> stands against the north wall (dark on the map; the “screen” light makes it blink). The “out of service” sign isn&#39;t painted on.</p>\n<p><strong>The passenger ramp.</strong> From the boarding door, the <strong>elevated walkway</strong>, glassed in on both sides, runs west: at its far end it rests on the ferry&#39;s stern. When the coterie enters the waiting room, <strong>Pell and Dawson are climbing the walkway</strong> (place them halfway along): they can be seen through the glass from the room. At the end of the walkway, the “Board the ferry” region leads to the stern deck of the passenger cabin (<code>ferry</code>). Boarding without Dawson seeing them: Dexterity + Stealth Diff. 4 against his Wits + Awareness (6 dice); Obfuscate doesn&#39;t fool his nose, but the wind off the Sound does (+1 die for the windward side: the wind comes in from the west, off the water).</p>\n<p><strong>The vehicle ramp</strong> (below, at dock level, in the southern strip): the vehicle holding lot and the ramp that crosses the water to the car deck. Anyone arriving by car (Dexterity + Drive Diff. 3 to get there before 12:55 a.m.) appears in the holding lot; the region at the end of the ramp leads to the stern of the car deck (<code>ferry-coches</code>). The east stairs go down to the street and the holding lot (twin regions on this same map), and the holding lot exits onto Alaskan Way (no map).</p>\n<p>The restrooms (hatched block) aren&#39;t played. The horn sounds at 12:50 a.m.: five minutes.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (1) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<div class=\"sbn-figuras\"><p><strong>Placed tokens.</strong> Hidden ones are revealed from the token layer; the ones that depend on how the night went say when.</p><ul><li>@UUID[Actor.eRE6FTNdGO76lzPK]{Mr. Pell} (A4-E03): Climbs the walkway slowly with the aluminum briefcase.</li><li>@UUID[Actor.Nq5NRC7yFhdkA5Er]{Dawson} (A4-E03): Pell leans on his arm; he looks back and sniffs the air.</li><li>@UUID[Actor.BzNGxOAK3F6Uo56T]{Security Guard 1} · <em>hidden</em> (A4-E03): The two ghouls with Dawson, ahead on the walkway.</li><li>@UUID[Actor.BzNGxOAK3F6Uo56T]{Security Guard 2} · <em>hidden</em> (A4-E03)</li><li>@UUID[Actor.ys08GDwMs80NuOlf]{Charles Halloway} · <em>hidden</em> (A4-E03): Only if he lost the vote or was exposed at the Council (A4-E01).</li></ul></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> Exit to Alaskan Way.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
